// Vec<PartDef>: parts Act 3 adds to the build (DESIGN.md L541-553, L565-570, L595, L618, L801-807, L866-875). Unit
// `data-act3`. Licensed CC BY 4.0.
//
// Act 3 opens part tier 5 (the tier 5 rows of parts/act1.ron, and the heavy guns here) and brings two families the
// first release lacks:
//
// Heavy guns, 130 to 155 mm (band Heavy: 150 mm at 1 km, 100 mm at 18 km, a 5-cell burst). They defeat the 80 mm
// armour tier at every range and reach 18 km, half again past the 127 mm. Mount weight and the 900 t cap gate them,
// with no hull-length rule (L551): the 130 mm single is a 30 t mount a 60 m corvette can carry forward, the 155 mm
// single 46 t and the twin 78 t, a tenth of a 900 t hull before its magazine. The 130 mm fires fastest of the three;
// the 155 mm mounts trade rate for weight of fire per hit and the tightest groups at range. Each feeds from its own
// calibre's magazine through the common hoist (L283). Rounds weigh shell plus charge (130 mm 50 kg, 155 mm 70 kg).
//
// The depth-charge rack, with the AI-only submarines (L551, L595): ten 180 kg charges rolled off the stern at 2 s
// intervals, two 5-charge patterns (the L618 gate's pattern) per rack, reloaded at the tender. A charge sinks at
// 3 m/s to its set depth (10 to 150 m, the Weapons officer sets it from the track) and bursts with B 8 and r 6
// cells. The rack sits at tier 4 so a player can fit one from the first day of the act, before any submarine is
// met. If submarines are cut from Act 3 (L875), this row goes with them.
//
// Units and conventions as parts/act1.ron: dry mass in kg (ammunition comes from the magazine rows and munitions),
// cost in Salvage, footprints in 0.5 m cells along (bow, up, starboard), power priorities from L287-295.
[
    // ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
